  "userdoc": {
    "kind": "user",
    "methods": {},
    "notice": "One append-only version log per document (keyed by genesis), with a         deal/offer layer over the SAME log — publishing and licensing are one         concern. Model:   - `makeOffer` is the single write authors use. It appends a version to the     log, then: whitelisted author (or safe) → the document becomes a DEAL     immediately; anyone else → it becomes a pending OFFER. An author can keep     calling `makeOffer` to edit while it is still an offer (each call appends     a version) before the publication agrees.   - `acceptOffer` (onlySafe) promotes an offer to a deal.   - `retract` is asymmetric: the author withdraws entirely (removed from     deals/offers); the publication (safe) demotes a deal back to an offer, or     rejects an offer.   - `hasDeal(genesis)` is the gate the Lit actions read. Identity is bytes32     everywhere; the string→bytes32 conversion is owned by `shared` and used     identically at write time and at the gate, so no on-chain cid map exists. Deals and offers are enumerable sets of genesis pointing into the one log; `getDeals`/`getOffers` read each entry's latest version via a cached pointer.",
    "version": 1
  }
